+    The walk starts at each drive-set bundle with a usable target, along its plain ``Depends
+    on`` and ``Depends on (merged)`` edges (those :func:`_runnable` holds on), then along
+    every edge kind of a prerequisite, and takes a COMPLETE bundle outside the drive set, a
+    finished named id included, deepest first. It stops at one with no patch (nothing to
+    merge) and at one for another target: merging that would not put it on the dependent's
+    base, so it is left alone and :func:`_runnable` holds the dependent.
+
+    Each one taken is merged (``merge._merge_one``, gates and all, ``merge_eligible`` being
+    the only licence to) when its record carries the marker, it is not merged yet, and its
+    own declared prerequisites are each merged into that base. A refusal, or anything
+    ``_merge_one`` raises, holds only its dependents: the run goes on, each message ending
+    with who is held. It runs once, before the waves: a split child adopted later is held,
+    not merged for."""
+    order: dict[str, tuple[Path, str, tuple[str, str]]] = {}   # deepest first: name → …
+    reach: dict[str, list[str]] = {}    # prerequisite name → the drive-set bundles waiting
